<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says 11-month coconut oil exports down.</title>
<headline>Manila says 11-month coconut oil exports down.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine coconut oil exports in the first 11 months of the year fell to 741,208 tonnes compared with 1,222,740 tonnes in the same period last year, trade group United Coconut Associations of the Phils Inc (UCAP) said.</p>
<p>Coconut products exports dropped 62 percent to 1,324,202 tonnes from January to November this year from the year-ago 2,146,148 tonnes, it said.</p>
<p>UCAP said coconut product exports include copra, coconut oil, dessicated coconut and oleochemicals.</p>
